1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:05,950
Every pet here is a real NYC 311 pothole complaint.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:10,950
Fixed means adopted, not found means ghost, waiting means feral.

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:16,950
Feral of the week: picked by the calendar, not by merit.

4
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:28,950
Filter by outcome and age. Hundreds of complaints have been open for over a year: that is the real backlog.

5
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:33,950
Each bio restates only facts from the city record.

6
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:39,950
Location is rounded to about 100 metres. No house numbers, ever.

7
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:46,950
The timeline: every change cites the record field that caused it.

8
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:51,950
The complaint history is the city's record, exactly as published.

9
00:00:52,000 --> 00:01:01,950
And here is that complaint on NYC Open Data. Nothing is invented.

10
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:09,950
Only 38 percent of complaints have coordinates, so the map holds fewer than half the shelter.

11
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:23,950
The rest are lost strays: complaints about a stretch of street between two cross streets. We list them by street instead of guessing a point.

12
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:33,950
The ghost hall: the city inspected and didn't find the reported problem. Not anyone's fault — potholes get patched, or move on.

13
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:48,950
Anyone can leave a pet an adoption note. It is filtered, rate-limited, and stored privately.

14
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:55,950
It stays private until a person approves it in the Shelter Office.

15
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:06,950
The sync log: last sync time, every run, and the unmapped phrases we refuse to guess.

16
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:17,950
The Office mirror: a live workflow for every open pet, and the review queues.

17
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:30,700
In the Shelter Office, a signed-in person approves the note. The workflow records who decided, and only then does the note appear on the pet’s page.

18
00:02:33,700 --> 00:02:38,700
Raw records stay untouched. Every fate is the city’s own.
